-- Help → Your account and household: the same text in 17 short paragraphs, one topic each, instead
-- of two (one of them some 3,200 characters). src/data/legalPages.json has the same. Only when the
-- section's paragraphs are still exactly the built-in ones, so an editor's rewording is left as it is.

update public.legal_pages p
set sections = (
      select jsonb_agg(
               case when s.elem->>'heading' = 'Your account and household' and s.elem->'paragraphs' = $lw$["Each person at home can have their own profile, with its own library and recommendations. Lock a profile with a PIN, set daily limits for younger readers, and change your plan, password or emails in Account. In Account → Sign-in you can add a passkey to log in with your face, fingerprint, screen lock or a security key instead of your password, and rename or remove passkeys you no longer use. You can cancel or pause online at any time. A Kids profile can ask for a book that isn't on its shelf; a grown-up says yes or no in Account → Family with the account password, and a yes opens that one book for that profile.", "Your plan includes some hours of audiobooks a month for the household (Premium has no limit) and a number of devices that can keep books offline. Account → Plan and billing shows how much you've used this month and which devices hold offline places, and lets you free one. To hear when a book you set Remind me on comes out, turn on Notifications on this device in Account → Preferences. Once it's on, choose there which notifications you get: books you're waiting for, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, an evening streak nudge, and answers to Kids book requests. On iPhone and iPad, add LiteraryWorm to your Home Screen first (Share, then Add to Home Screen) and turn them on in the app. Grown-up and teen profiles can put a book on the family shelf from its page; it shows on Home for everyone at home, and Kids profiles see only the books their rating already allows. On a book club's page, Where everyone is shows the chapter each member has reached, for members who turn on Show my place to this club; it's off until you turn it on. Under a club's discussion, Shared highlights shows passages members marked in the book; ones from chapters you haven't reached stay hidden until you choose to see them. Share one of yours from the list there, with or without its note, and stop sharing it whenever you like. My Library → Smart lists fill themselves: Almost there (past halfway), Waiting for you (started, not opened for 30 days), From authors you follow and Loved it. A book's page shows Your time with this book once you've read or listened to it: time spent, the days, your pace through it and your biggest days. In the player (and the mini-player's More), Previously… catches you up on a public-domain book from the second chapter on: the story so far and the last chapter, written by AI from the chapters before yours only. My Library → Notes has Review for highlights: each comes back the day after you make it, then after 1, 3, 7, 14, 30 and 60 days while it still matters, up to 10 a day, and Home says when some are due. On a book's page, Reading plan lets you pick a day to finish by: it works out about how many minutes (at your own pace) or pages a day get you there, and says whether you're on track, ahead or behind; Home lists your plans. When you buy a gift on Gifts, you can add up to 10 LiteraryWorm books to it (find a title, or add one of your lists); they're waiting in the recipient's library when they redeem it. To take your library elsewhere, choose Export for Goodreads or Export for StoryGraph in My Library: you get a CSV of your books, shelves, star ratings (Love it 5, Like it 4, Not for me 2) and dates, made on your device, to import there. In the reader, Display has OpenDyslexic among the fonts, and Reading guide: a reading ruler on one line, or line focus, which dims everything but three lines. It follows your pointer or a tap; J and K move it down or up a line. On an audiobook's page, Read offline has Listen offline on a schedule: this device keeps the chapter you're on and the next 1, 3, 5 or 10 as you listen, on Wi-Fi only if you like, and can remove chapters you've finished. It counts as one of your plan's offline devices."]$lw$::jsonb
                    then jsonb_set(s.elem, '{paragraphs}', $lw$["Each person at home can have their own profile, with its own library and recommendations. Lock a profile with a PIN, set daily limits for younger readers, and change your plan, password or emails in Account. You can cancel or pause online at any time.", "In Account → Sign-in you can add a passkey to log in with your face, fingerprint, screen lock or a security key instead of your password, and rename or remove passkeys you no longer use.", "A Kids profile can ask for a book that isn't on its shelf; a grown-up says yes or no in Account → Family with the account password, and a yes opens that one book for that profile.", "Your plan includes some hours of audiobooks a month for the household (Premium has no limit) and a number of devices that can keep books offline. Account → Plan and billing shows how much you've used this month and which devices hold offline places, and lets you free one.", "To hear when a book you set Remind me on comes out, turn on Notifications on this device in Account → Preferences. Once it's on, choose there which notifications you get: books you're waiting for, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, an evening streak nudge, and answers to Kids book requests. On iPhone and iPad, add LiteraryWorm to your Home Screen first (Share, then Add to Home Screen) and turn them on in the app.", "Grown-up and teen profiles can put a book on the family shelf from its page; it shows on Home for everyone at home, and Kids profiles see only the books their rating already allows.", "On a book club's page, Where everyone is shows the chapter each member has reached, for members who turn on Show my place to this club; it's off until you turn it on.", "Under a club's discussion, Shared highlights shows passages members marked in the book; ones from chapters you haven't reached stay hidden until you choose to see them. Share one of yours from the list there, with or without its note, and stop sharing it whenever you like.", "My Library → Smart lists fill themselves: Almost there (past halfway), Waiting for you (started, not opened for 30 days), From authors you follow and Loved it.", "A book's page shows Your time with this book once you've read or listened to it: time spent, the days, your pace through it and your biggest days.", "In the player (and the mini-player's More), Previously… catches you up on a public-domain book from the second chapter on: the story so far and the last chapter, written by AI from the chapters before yours only.", "My Library → Notes has Review for highlights: each comes back the day after you make it, then after 1, 3, 7, 14, 30 and 60 days while it still matters, up to 10 a day, and Home says when some are due.", "On a book's page, Reading plan lets you pick a day to finish by: it works out about how many minutes (at your own pace) or pages a day get you there, and says whether you're on track, ahead or behind; Home lists your plans.", "When you buy a gift on Gifts, you can add up to 10 LiteraryWorm books to it (find a title, or add one of your lists); they're waiting in the recipient's library when they redeem it.", "To take your library elsewhere, choose Export for Goodreads or Export for StoryGraph in My Library: you get a CSV of your books, shelves, star ratings (Love it 5, Like it 4, Not for me 2) and dates, made on your device, to import there.", "In the reader, Display has OpenDyslexic among the fonts, and Reading guide: a reading ruler on one line, or line focus, which dims everything but three lines. It follows your pointer or a tap; J and K move it down or up a line.", "On an audiobook's page, Read offline has Listen offline on a schedule: this device keeps the chapter you're on and the next 1, 3, 5 or 10 as you listen, on Wi-Fi only if you like, and can remove chapters you've finished. It counts as one of your plan's offline devices."]$lw$::jsonb)
                    else s.elem end
               order by s.ord)
      from jsonb_array_elements(p.sections) with ordinality as s(elem, ord)
    ),
    updated_at = now()
where p.slug = 'help'
  and jsonb_typeof(p.sections) = 'array'
  and exists (
    select 1 from jsonb_array_elements(p.sections) e
    where e->>'heading' = 'Your account and household' and e->'paragraphs' = $lw$["Each person at home can have their own profile, with its own library and recommendations. Lock a profile with a PIN, set daily limits for younger readers, and change your plan, password or emails in Account. In Account → Sign-in you can add a passkey to log in with your face, fingerprint, screen lock or a security key instead of your password, and rename or remove passkeys you no longer use. You can cancel or pause online at any time. A Kids profile can ask for a book that isn't on its shelf; a grown-up says yes or no in Account → Family with the account password, and a yes opens that one book for that profile.", "Your plan includes some hours of audiobooks a month for the household (Premium has no limit) and a number of devices that can keep books offline. Account → Plan and billing shows how much you've used this month and which devices hold offline places, and lets you free one. To hear when a book you set Remind me on comes out, turn on Notifications on this device in Account → Preferences. Once it's on, choose there which notifications you get: books you're waiting for, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, an evening streak nudge, and answers to Kids book requests. On iPhone and iPad, add LiteraryWorm to your Home Screen first (Share, then Add to Home Screen) and turn them on in the app. Grown-up and teen profiles can put a book on the family shelf from its page; it shows on Home for everyone at home, and Kids profiles see only the books their rating already allows. On a book club's page, Where everyone is shows the chapter each member has reached, for members who turn on Show my place to this club; it's off until you turn it on. Under a club's discussion, Shared highlights shows passages members marked in the book; ones from chapters you haven't reached stay hidden until you choose to see them. Share one of yours from the list there, with or without its note, and stop sharing it whenever you like. My Library → Smart lists fill themselves: Almost there (past halfway), Waiting for you (started, not opened for 30 days), From authors you follow and Loved it. A book's page shows Your time with this book once you've read or listened to it: time spent, the days, your pace through it and your biggest days. In the player (and the mini-player's More), Previously… catches you up on a public-domain book from the second chapter on: the story so far and the last chapter, written by AI from the chapters before yours only. My Library → Notes has Review for highlights: each comes back the day after you make it, then after 1, 3, 7, 14, 30 and 60 days while it still matters, up to 10 a day, and Home says when some are due. On a book's page, Reading plan lets you pick a day to finish by: it works out about how many minutes (at your own pace) or pages a day get you there, and says whether you're on track, ahead or behind; Home lists your plans. When you buy a gift on Gifts, you can add up to 10 LiteraryWorm books to it (find a title, or add one of your lists); they're waiting in the recipient's library when they redeem it. To take your library elsewhere, choose Export for Goodreads or Export for StoryGraph in My Library: you get a CSV of your books, shelves, star ratings (Love it 5, Like it 4, Not for me 2) and dates, made on your device, to import there. In the reader, Display has OpenDyslexic among the fonts, and Reading guide: a reading ruler on one line, or line focus, which dims everything but three lines. It follows your pointer or a tap; J and K move it down or up a line. On an audiobook's page, Read offline has Listen offline on a schedule: this device keeps the chapter you're on and the next 1, 3, 5 or 10 as you listen, on Wi-Fi only if you like, and can remove chapters you've finished. It counts as one of your plan's offline devices."]$lw$::jsonb
  );
